This project has a graphify knowledge graph at graphify-out/.

- Before answering architecture or codebase questions, read graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md for god nodes and community structure
- If graphify-out/wiki/index.md exists, navigate it instead of reading raw files
- After modifying code files in this session, run `graphify update .` to keep the graph current (AST-only, no API cost)

## Per-package graphs

This repo uses package-level graphs. Per-package GRAPH_REPORT.md files are at:
graphify-out/<package>/GRAPH_REPORT.md

Packages: BusinessLogicModule, ConfigurationModule, ConnectionModule,
ConverterModule, Infrastructure, LoggingModule, Pms_GuidanceGUI.exe,
Pms_GuidanceGUI.Tests, Upgrade

Prefer the package-specific report when working inside a single module.
Use `python -m graphify query "<q>" --graph graphify-out/<pkg>/graph.json` for deep queries.
For cross-module questions, use the merged graph: `graphify-out/merged.json`
Rebuild: `bash scripts/graphify.sh PKG=<name>` or `.\scripts\Invoke-Graphify.ps1 -Package <name>`
Merge only: `bash scripts/graphify.sh --merge-only` or `.\scripts\Invoke-Graphify.ps1 -MergeOnly`

## MCP server

An MCP server is configured in `.mcp.json` (server: `graphify`).
Tools available: `query_graph`, `get_node`, `get_neighbors`, `shortest_path`
Start: `python -m graphify.serve graphify-out/merged.json` or `make graphify-mcp`
